A||||6||RobertVol||Weird feeling in the Stick||||5||
Z||000000||RobertVol||05-05-2000||12:06 AM||||OK Guys.....I tried to explain this once before but wasnt very accurate in my post. <P>Has anybody felt like something bumping in your stick or maybe in the front of the car right when you first accelerate or when coming to almost a stop like when slowing for a spped bump and then after passing the bump speeding up and like a rod or something moving that you feel in the stick? I cant really explain it but I can feel it in the stick. Also when hard braking ..right at the point of a complete stop letting off the brake peddle quickly and you can feel it in the stick!! I know this is a very cloudy description but I just dont know how to explain without driving it. But seems to be in sudden stops then acceleration that does it. Could be a tie rod? My performance is great and no symptoms of bad suspension. Any suggestions would be great. This car is my 88GT. its only got 28k on it so it should not be too much wrong !!<P>This is just one of those things thats more nagging thing than major but get real irritating||||reg||5
Z||000001||Terrybogin||05-05-2000||12:40 AM||||Motor/tranny mounts maybe?||||reg||1
Z||000002||RobertVol||05-05-2000||12:46 AM||||I know its not the Motor but tranny hmmm I will have to check that but does not FEEL like that. This may sound weird but it seems to off in the front but feeling through to the stick ||||reg||1
Z||000003||RobertVol||05-05-2000||12:48 AM||||I know some have talked replacing the shifter cable...what was the reason? Maybe thats the problem||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||05-05-2000||09:40 AM||||This is kind of a strech, but based on the fact that you notice the problem when you first start to move and then when you are stopping, you may want to check your brakes.  You can feel alot of stuff through that shifter.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||05-05-2000||10:06 AM||||If you feel it at the stick at start or stop it sounds to me that something may be hitting/pulling/pushing one of the shifting cables. If it has 28K miles mounts should be OK but a screw may be loose. Check them all including the dog bone. That one makes the engine rock very hard. Also check the rear suspension. Whatever it is I'm almost sure it should be in the engine compartment. Don't forget the battery. Is heavy and maybe loose and rocking.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ROB MAC||05-05-2000||08:33 PM||||Maybe a brake caliper is sticking and the pad shifting as you move . I cleaned up mine and my "bump" went away. The piston was awful cruddy.||||reg||1
